            <ArticleTitle>[Markers of chronic inflammation in patients with ischemic heart disease with in-stent restenosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Concentrations of interleukins 6 and 10, tumor necrosis factor alpha, transforming growth factor beta and C-reactive protein were measured in 42 patients before and in remote period after coronary stenting. Patients with angiographically documented in-stent restenosis compared with those without restenosis had higher initial levels of interleukin 6 and more often discontinued therapy with statins.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
